From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: opt-in redundant resize guard and origin diagnostics

Separate tester-only patch on top of 0070/0071. Default off, no UI or
normal-release change. Keep forced rebuilds and existing feedback resets.
Log provenance without claiming sender attribution or physical recovery.

---
diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index ce407e53b..7a21984cc 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -6480,6 +6480,22 @@ them.
     samples/feedback are not evidence of black output. S_OK/counters do not prove
     physical display output. Capture overhead must be evaluated on the test PC.
 
+``--d3d11-skip-redundant-resize=<yes|no>``
+    Diagnostic-only mpv-ht A/B test (default: no). Restart the player after
+    changing it. Skip ordinary same-size notification buffer resizes only when
+    the queried swapchain, window, monitor and output state are unchanged and
+    healthy. Unknown origins, actual size/state changes, explicit configuration,
+    fullscreen transitions and recovery paths still perform the resize.
+    Window notification handling and existing feedback resets are unchanged.
+    This is not a proven blackout fix. No UI control or automatic recovery.
+
+    This option or blackout diagnostics also enables bounded resize-origin and
+    decision logging. With the recorder enabled, decisions enter its JSONL
+    history. Origin messages include a numeric action and sanitized setting-area
+    name, not the sending process identity. A skip has no resize_begin/resize_end
+    pair because no ResizeBuffers call was made. Use the same engine with this
+    flag set to no/yes/no for controlled A/B/A comparison.
+
 ``--d3d11-blackout-dir=<path>``
     Recorder destination (default: ``~~/../user-data/logs/blackout``). Used only
     with blackout diagnostics enabled. Retains the four newest owned JSONL files,
